    "overview": "ISO/IEC 29100 is the international privacy framework from ISO and IEC. It fixes a common privacy vocabulary, names the actors involved in processing personally identifiable information \u2014 PII principal, PII controller, PII processor and third party \u2014 explains how to recognise PII and derive privacy safeguarding requirements, and sets out eleven privacy principles. It is not certifiable; it is the reference that ISO/IEC 27701, 27018 and 29151 are built on, and it is available free of charge.",
